{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "A1",
  "unit": 25,
  "title": "Sweets and snacks",
  "description": "Name the sweet things, and say what you like to eat.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "Sweets are a small set of nouns, and they are the first words a learner uses to say what they like. The grammar is the same as everywhere else: a gender, an article, and the plural.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The nouns",
        "body": "La galleta, la mermelada, la nata and la patata frita are feminine. El caramelo, el pastel, el chicle, el yogur and el cacahuete are masculine. El cacahuete is a good one to notice: it is a nut in a pod, and it is masculine.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "la galleta",
            "en": "the biscuit"
          },
          {
            "es": "el caramelo",
            "en": "the sweet"
          },
          {
            "es": "el yogur",
            "en": "the yoghurt"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "What you like",
        "body": "You know how to say what a thing is for, and how to ask for one with un or una: una galleta, un caramelo, un yogur. The plural works the same: las galletas and los caramelos.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "quiero una galleta",
            "en": "I want a biscuit"
          },
          {
            "es": "los caramelos son buenos",
            "en": "the sweets are good"
          },
          {
            "es": "el pastel es de chocolate",
            "en": "the cake is chocolate"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
